  "result": "I added `compareVersions(a, b)` in `src/cli/semver.ts` and committed it as 235b1e6. `npm run fast` passed, covering Biome, the import-boundary check, `tsc` and the related tests.\n\n- **Ordering:** it returns -1, 0 or 1. It compares each dotted part numerically, so `1.10.0` sorts above `1.9.0`. Missing trailing parts count as 0, so `1.2` equals `1.2.0`.\n- **Invalid input:** a part that isn't all digits, such as `1.x`, makes it throw `invalid version`. You didn't specify this case, so say if you'd rather it return something else.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/semver.test.ts` uses `node:test` and covers equality, numeric versus lexical ordering, missing parts and the throw. I added its weight to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n\nThe commit title ends with `(t-mpu3w44)` and the commit carries a `Ticket: t-mpu3w44` trailer. I did not touch `tasks/t-mpu3w44.json`, since only the lead changes task status.",
